extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 18: Mystic Russia pp.61-63, read from the text layer. IMPORTED UNDER D4. NO xp_table, per D3. ''ALL LEVEL ONE EARTH WARLOCK SPELLS'' IS ENUMERATED RATHER THAN GATED: spell_traditions_allowed governs a LEVEL-GATED pick and this is an outright grant, so the eleven level-one Earth rows the catalog holds are named - Chameleon, Create Wood, Dowsing, Dust Storm, Fool''s Gold, Identify Minerals, Identify Plants, Mystic Fulcrum, Rock to Mud, Rot Wood, Shatter - and the list was read off production, not off the book, so it grants what this catalog actually has. The four named warlock spells that follow it also resolve only under the Earth: prefix: Wither Plants, Grow Plants, Mend Stone and Travel Through Walls have NO unprefixed rows, and Travel Through Walls in particular sits beside a separate Earth: Travel Through Stone. Note the class therefore grants BOTH Chameleon and Earth: Chameleon, which is what the book does - the general invocation is named in its own list and the Earth one arrives with the level-one sweep. THE BOOK SEPARATES ''Natural Abilities'' FROM ''R.C.C. Skills'' AND THIS IMPORT KEEPS THAT SEAM: prowl, climb, swim and the tracking percentages are recorded as prose. THE MIDDAY DOUBLING IS NOT STORED - M.D.C. and Spd both double between noon and 3 p.m. and the app holds one number per pool, so both stay at their ordinary figures and the doubling is a natural ability. Two metric conversions in this entry are wrong in the book (300 feet given as 61.5 m, where the Domovoi''s same figure is 91.5 m) and the feet are carried. The +25% is for SELECTED skills only. The text layer carries this book''s digit cipher: the M.D.C. line prints ''+2D4xlO'' and the S.D.C.-world line ''!D4xlO''."
