# Polevoi

## Lore

The Polevoi is the spirit of the field: a four-foot humanoid the colour of the
earth, with long stringy grass or leafy green hair, brown eyes and clothes woven
from vines. It carries a walking stick, a sickle or a scythe, and sometimes
those are enchanted.

It is anarchist and spiteful, bold, arrogant, self-absorbed, easily provoked and
quick to lash out. It has little tolerance for humans or for stupidity, and it
is known for playing mean and often deadly jokes.

It is called the Midday Spirit because that is when it is strongest. Between
noon and three in the afternoon its M.D.C. doubles, its speed doubles, and its
magic jumps from third-level potency to sixth.

## Alignment

Any, but the majority are anarchist (55%), miscreant (20%) or unprincipled
(10%) - the most evil-leaning spread of the six.

## GM Notes

**The book talks a player out of this one while permitting it.** The Player
Note allows a Polevoi as an optional character and then spends a paragraph
saying it will wander off, insult the party, provoke brawls, and act like a
spoiled child - closing with *"probably more trouble than it is worth."*

Against that: it is resourceful, adventurous, afraid of nobody, a reasonably
good fighter and a genuinely good user of magic. It has no love for demons,
witches or necromancers. Most make good scouts, spies and thieves.

Keep the visits to town short. The book recommends **one to four days** before
the mischief starts.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'polevoi');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'polevoi';

